id:                     E2167
trigger_tool:           make|python|test
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        AttributeError: do_dlsym failed: Symbol not found.*so=/data/service/hnp/bin/python3|FAIL: .*test_python\.py
severity:               3
category:               security, platform, ohos, autotools, testing
match_keywords:         ctypes, CDLL(None), PY_LOG_COMPILER, embedded python, launcher, make check PYTHON, dlopen, isl_test_python, Py_DecodeLocale, python3-config --embed
title:                  Route upstream dlopen/ctypes tests past the OHOS worker loader boundary with an embedded-Python launcher that links the library under test as its own NEEDED
prescan_pattern:        ctypes\.CDLL\(|cdll\.LoadLibrary\(
prescan_globs:          *.py, *.py.in, *.py.top, Makefile*, *.mk
root_cause:              On workers where dlopen and LD_PRELOAD refuse user-directory shared objects (E2166), the only loader path that accepts them is the process-startup DT_NEEDED chain. A tiny embedded-Python launcher whose own NEEDED entry is the freshly self-signed library under test maps it into the process global symbol scope before the interpreter initializes, so the upstream ctypes binding resolves through its CDLL(None) fallback and the real test logic executes unchanged. The stock interpreter can never do this because no post-start mapping of the library is permitted there.
affected_scope:         Any archived package whose upstream suite contains ctypes/FFI tests against a shared library built in the same conan build (python bindings, plugin-loading tests).
verification_cmd:       make -n check shows PY_LOG_COMPILER expanding to the launcher; then one upstream test executed through it passes while the same interpreter name via stock python3 fails on dlopen (worker evidence: PR #6848 build #33932 flipped isl_test_python.py from FAIL to PASS).
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           embedded-python-launcher
rec_description:        Compile launcher.c (Py_Initialize, Py_DecodeLocale-marshalled argv, script-dir sys.path insertion, PyRun_SimpleFileEx) with clang linking the freshly self-signed shared library by full path (NEEDED records the SONAME) plus HNP libpython (rpath to its directory; python3-config --embed fallback when no shared libpython exists); route the automake test through it with make check PYTHON=<launcher>.
rec_command:            clang -Wno-deprecated-declarations launcher.c -I "$($PY -c import\ sysconfig\;print\(sysconfig.get_paths\(\)\[.include.\]\)") <PYROOT>/lib/libpython3.12.so <selfsigned>/<libtarget.so> -Wl,-rpath,<PYROOT>/lib -o launcher && make -j1 check PYTHON="$PWD/launcher"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      python3-config-embed-static
fallback_description:   Executors whose HNP python ships no libpython.so (Py_ENABLE_SHARED=0): compile with python3-config --includes plus --ldflags --embed so the interpreter links statically; the library-under-test NEEDED entry is unchanged.
fallback_command:       clang launcher.c $(python3-config --includes) <selfsigned>/libtarget.so $(python3-config --ldflags --embed) -o launcher
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       (export )?PYTHON=[^ ]+ &&? .*make .*check|PYTHON=[^ ]+ make
forbid_1_reason:        A shell environment prefix PYTHON=... is overridden by the configure-generated assignment PYTHON = @PYTHON@ in the Makefile; build #33918 proved the stock interpreter silently kept running the test (traceback so=/data/service/hnp/bin/python3) while the launcher was built and never used. Only a make command-line variable overrides the assignment and propagates through recursive makes.
forbid_1_consequence:   Expensive CI rounds spent on a fallback that is actually dead code.
forbid_2_pattern:       LD_PRELOAD=.*(make|ctest).*check
forbid_2_reason:        Workers ignore LD_PRELOAD of user-directory libraries (E2166, build #33895); the preloaded object never joins the global scope and the test still fails at CDLL(None) with a misleading missing-symbol error.
forbid_2_consequence:   Misattribution of the failure to the launcher or the signature instead of the loader policy.
forbid_3_pattern:       argv-as-wchar|PySys_SetArgvEx\(.*argv \+ 1, 0\)(?![\s\S]*Py_DecodeLocale)
forbid_3_reason:        Passing char** argv directly to PySys_SetArgvEx corrupts sys.argv (wchar_t re-interpretation of char* produced fatal 'no mem for sys.argv' and out-of-range codepoint errors before the fix); argv must be marshalled through Py_DecodeLocale.
forbid_3_consequence:   Launcher crashes before the first test line, indistinguishable from a loader policy failure in truncated logs.
principles:             
causes:                 []
caused_by:              [E2166]
similar_to:             [E2164, E135]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        
